ame></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIMADA HIROYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKIZAWA TERUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMADA, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKIZAWA, TERUO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A semiconductor device including an insulated-gate field-effect transistor has a gate electrode whose work function is well controlled to be close to the intrinsic mid-gap energy of silicon to reduce impurity concentration in the channel.  The insulated-gate field-effect transistor thus prevents the carrier mobility from decreasing and provides higher current-carrying capacity.  The gate electrode has a multilayer structure including a p-type polycrystalline or single-crystal germanium film (3) and a low-resistivity conductor film (4).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un dispositif à semi-conducteur incluant un transistor à effet de champ à grille isolée. Le dispositif à semi-conducteur comprend une gâchette dont la fonction de travail est bien contrôlée de manière à être proche de l'énergie intrinsèque du silicium au niveau du semi-écartement des contacts, cela, afin de réduire la concentration d'impuretés dans le canal. Ainsi, le transistor à effet de champ à grille isolée empêche un ralentissement de la mobilité de porteur de charge et offre une intensité de courant admissible supérieure. La gâchette présente une structure multicouches comprenant une couche au germanium polycristalline ou monocristalline de type p (3) et une couche conductrice (4) à faible résistivité.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>